-- title:
--   1-ζ is a uniformiser when v(q)=q-1
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring that is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, let $q$ be a prime number, and let $\zeta \in A$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity in the sense of Mathlib's `IsPrimitiveRoot`. Suppose $\varpi \in A$ generates the maximal ideal of $A$, that is, $\mathrm{maximalIdeal}\ A = (\varpi)$, and suppose there is a unit $\varepsilon \in A$ with $\varpi^{\,q-1} = \varepsilon\, q$, where $q$ denotes the image of the natural number $q$ in $A$; thus $q$ has valuation exactly $q-1$. The conclusion is that there exists $u \in A$ which is a unit and satisfies $1 - \zeta = u\,\varpi$. In other words, $1-\zeta$ is itself a uniformiser of $A$, associated to $\varpi$; equivalently the maximal ideal of $A$ is generated by $1-\zeta$.
--
--   This is the standard fact from the theory of cyclotomic fields that, in a discrete valuation ring in which the rational prime $q$ has valuation $q-1$, the element $1-\zeta$ attached to a primitive $q$-th root of unity generates the maximal ideal. It is used in the analysis of the local structure of modular curves of full level at $q$, in particular in the computations of completions of local rings and their residue rings appearing in the study of $q$-adic unramifiedness and reducedness.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsPrimitiveRoot_exists_isUnit_one_sub_eq_mul_of_pow_sub_one_eq_mul.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
